poke
------------------------------------------
GNU poke is an interactive, extensible editor for binary data. Not limited to
editing basic entities such as bits and bytes, it provides a full-fledged
procedural, interactive programming language designed to describe data
structures and to operate on them.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgc1-8.2.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libintl8-0.22.5-1
  libncursesw10-6.5+20240427-1
  libpoke-devel-5.0-1bl1
  libpoke2-5.0-1bl1
  libreadline8-8.3-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  dejagnu-1.6.3-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gettext-devel-0.22.5-1
  libgc-devel-8.2.12-1
  libintl-devel-0.22.5-1
  libncurses-devel-6.5+20240427-1
  libreadline-devel-8.3-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://www.jemarch.net/poke

Canonical download:
  mirror://gnu/poke/poke-5.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack poke-5.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./poke-5.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/poke-5.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/poke-5.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpoke2-5.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpoke-devel-5.0-X.tar.xz

